---
import LabShell from "../../components/lab/LabShell.astro";
import ProjectCard from "../../components/ProjectCard.astro";
import ServiceCard from "../../components/ServiceCard.astro";
import TeamCard from "../../components/TeamCard.astro";
import Tile from "../../components/Tile.astro";
---
<LabShell title="Cards" current="cards"
  intro="Four card-shaped molecules, all built on the .card primitive (global.css §6.3) but diverging in props and — in two cases — never actually used. Body copy in every card runs on .card__text (var(--copy-md), 17px) — the M tier of the copy scale, see Typography — one step down from the page's regular reading copy.">

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--unused">unused on real pages</span>
    <h2>ProjectCard <span class="lab-source" style="display:inline;">vs.</span> ServiceCard</h2>
    <p>Nearly identical: title + body + link on <code>.card</code>. <code>ProjectCard</code> is used by
      <code>NetworkSection</code> (the Regenerant Catalunya cohort pages). <code>ServiceCard</code> has zero
      usages anywhere — <code>what-we-do.astro</code> doesn't render it, despite the name suggesting that's
      where it belongs. Candidate to merge into one <code>Card</code> with an <code>external</code> prop,
      once it's clear whether what-we-do actually needs the extra field ProjectCard has.</p>
    <div class="lab-grid">
      <ProjectCard title="Project card" body="title + body + 'Read case study →' or 'See site ↗' if external." href="#" />
      <ServiceCard title="Service card" body="title + body + 'Learn more →'. Currently unused anywhere." href="#" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--live">live</span>
    <h2>TeamCard</h2>
    <p>No portrait photos exist, so the visual anchor is an Averia monogram over a pillar-tinted Aurora
      header — a deliberate placeholder pattern, not a fallback for a missing feature.</p>
    <p class="lab-source">Used in: about.astro and index.astro (team roster)</p>
    <div class="lab-grid">
      <TeamCard name="Jane Doe" role="Coordination" pillar="tissue" bio="Short bio line, one or two sentences." />
      <TeamCard name="Alex Roig" role="Finance" pillar="flow" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--unused">unused on real pages</span>
    <h2>Tile</h2>
    <p>Link tile with eyebrow + title + body + status footer. Fully built, zero usages found — looks aimed
      at a directory/index-style layout (commons? atlas index?) that hasn't been built with it yet.</p>
    <div class="lab-grid">
      <Tile href="#" eyebrow="Category" title="Tile title" body="Supporting body copy for the tile." status="Status footer" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-note">
    <strong>Gap:</strong> three of four card variants here are either unused (<code>ServiceCard</code>,
    <code>Tile</code>) or have an unused sibling (<code>ProjectCard</code>/<code>ServiceCard</code>). Before
    adding a fifth card variant anywhere, worth consolidating these first.
  </div>
</LabShell>
